&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Section 1833(e) of the Social Security Act precludes payment to any provider of services unless &quot;there has been furnished such information as may be necessary in order to determine the amounts due such provider.&quot; It is expected that the beneficiary&#39;s medical records will reflect the need for the care provided. The beneficiary&#39;s medical records include the treating practitioner&#39;s office records, hospital records, nursing home records, home health agency records, records from other healthcare professionals and test reports. This documentation must be available upon request.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GENERAL DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;In order to justify payment for DMEPOS items, suppliers must meet the following requirements:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SWO&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Medical Record Information (including continued need&sol;use if applicable)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Correct Coding&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proof of Delivery&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Refer to the LCD-related Standard Documentation Requirements article, located at the bottom of this policy under the Related Local Coverage Documents section for additional information regarding these requirements.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Refer to the Supplier Manual for additional information on documentation requirements.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Refer to the DME MAC web sites for additional bulletin articles and other publications related to this LCD.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POLICY SPECIFIC DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Items covered in this LCD have additional policy-specific requirements that must be met to justify&amp;nbsp;Medicare reimbursement. &lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Refer to the LCD-related Policy article, located at the bottom of this policy under the Related Local Coverage Documents section for additional information.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Miscellaneous&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Appendices&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Utilization Guidelines&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Refer to Coverage Indications, Limitations and&sol;or Medical Necessity&lt;&sol;p&gt;

